{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qf7UXQBfAGsa3YZV8znoDQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024\"},{\"title\":\"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up\",\"url\":\"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/\"},{\"title\":\"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024's instructions for reviews. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. Specifically:\n- Formatting issues involve papers that are either too long or in an incorrect format.\n- Anonymity violation occurs when the main manuscript, supplemental materials, or a link provided in a paper identifies one or more of the authors.\n- Regarding scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search results from the official CoRL 2024 instructions page provided these review guidelines, though the complete scoring scale and detailed rating criteria appear to require viewing the full page directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de8902b1-95db-4d6b-992d-38f39dba7b46","uuid":"b0c1189f-12f1-4800-9d4e-b6b54aabeebf","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:18:09.874Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VZVhrbRbY6mGuvYTcZ5B4v","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery","url":"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024"},{"title":"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up","url":"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/"},{"title":"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024's instructions for reviews. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Review Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. Specifically:\n- Formatting issues involve papers that are either too long or in an incorrect format.\n- Anonymity violation occurs when the main manuscript, supplemental materials, or a link provided in a paper identifies one or more of the authors.\n- Regarding scope, all CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nThe search results from the official CoRL 2024 instructions page provided these review guidelines, though the complete scoring scale and detailed rating criteria appear to require viewing the full page directly."],"durationSeconds":5.704603831999997}}
