{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvBdkDESMmvaKoTiNf7AoR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL openreview review form \"Overall Rating\" \"Strong Accept\" \"Accept\" \"Borderline\" \"Reject\"\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://virtual.aistats.org/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://www.auai.org/uai2023/reviewing_instructions\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Training Material\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerTrainingMaterial\"},{\"title\":\"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137\"}]\n\nI found information about OpenReview review forms and general conference review rating scales. However, the search results don't contain specific information about CoRL's particular OpenReview review form with the exact \"Overall Rating\" options you mentioned.\n\nFrom the search results, I can see that:\n\n- OpenReview's default review form uses a rating scale with options like \"9: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\" and \"7: Good paper, accept\"\n- Several conferences (AISTATS, UAI, ICML) use rating scales that include options like \"Borderline Accept,\" \"Borderline Reject,\" and \"Reject\"\n- For CoRL 2026, papers that receive all reviews in the \"reject\" range in the initial round will not proc