se / degenerate policies\n6. **Questions for Authors**\n7. **Significance & Novelty Score** (1-4)\n8. **Presentation Score** (1-4)\n9. **Overall Rating** (1-10, CoRL scale)\n10. **Confidence** (1-5)\n11. **One-line summary of review**\n\nBe rigorous on novelty. Consider: (a) Is the observation that a frozen robot gets high CAR really novel, or is it an obvious failure mode that practitioners would catch? (b) Is dfCAR a significant methodological contribution or essentially \"check if the robot moved\"? (c) Is the SDF redundancy finding specific to the EE-only formulation and thus unsurprising? (d) Does the paper oversell findings from a narrow experimental scope (2 model families, 1 benchmark, simulation only)?\n","uuid":"84a2ea3e-82e7-4530-a34b-19b24b6fa661","session_id":"de8902b1-95db-4d6b-992d-38f39dba7b46"}
